  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A Binod is a person who is very good with bitwise operations. Help Alice solve the following problem and become a Binod.\n\nYou are given an array AAA of NNN elements. Process QQQ queries on this array, of the following form:\n\n\nEach query contains 555 integers k,L1,R1,L2,R2k, L_1, R_1, L_2, R_2k,L1​,R1​,L2​,R2​. It is guaranteed that L1≤R1&lt;L2≤R2L_1 \\leq R_1 \\lt L_2 \\leq R_2L1​≤R1​&lt;L2​≤R2​.\nThe answer to a query is the number of pairs (i,j)(i, j)(i,j) such that:\n\nL1≤i≤R1L_1 \\leq i \\leq R_1L1​≤i≤R1​ and L2≤j≤R2L_2 \\leq j \\leq R_2L2​≤j≤R2​\nAi⊕AjA_i \\oplus A_jAi​⊕Aj​ has its kkk-th bit set. Here ⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes the bitwise XOR operation.\n\n\n**Note:** An integer xxx is said to have its kkk-th bit set if the (unique) binary representation of xxx contains 2k2^k2k. For example, 5=1012=20+225 = 101_2 = 2^0 + 2^25=1012​=20+22 has its zeroth and second bits set but not the first, while 16=100002=2416 = 10000_2 = 2^416=100002​=24 has only its fourth bit set.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and QQQ — the number of elements in array and number of queries, respectively.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nThe next QQQ lines describe queries. The iii-th of these QQQ lines contains 555 space-separated integers k,L1,R1,L2,R2k, L_1, R_1, L_2, R_2k,L1​,R1​,L2​,R2​ — the parameters described in the statement.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output QQQ lines.The iii-th of these lines should be the answer to the iii-th query.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤5⋅1041 \\leq T \\leq 5 \\cdot 10^41≤T≤5⋅104",
      "2≤N≤1052 \\leq N \\leq 10^52≤N≤105",
      "1≤Q≤5⋅1051 \\leq Q \\leq 5\\cdot 10^51≤Q≤5⋅105",
      "0≤Ai&lt;2600 \\leq A_i \\lt 2^{60}0≤Ai​&lt;260",
      "1≤L1≤R1&lt;L2≤R2≤N1 \\leq L_1 \\leq R_1 \\lt L_2 \\leq R_2 \\leq N1≤L1​≤R1​&lt;L2​≤R2​≤N.",
      "0≤k&lt;600 \\leq k \\lt 600≤k&lt;60",
      "The sum of NNN and QQQ over all test cases won't exceed 10510^5105 and 5⋅1055\\cdot 10^55⋅105 respectively."
    ],
